{"source_key":"sha256-9c05c90c85130596b57f728558108305","record_index":168,"record_hash":"sha256:17b9eca11b9abae6bf533c2a43d993b9a296ed8cb68cbd2d96a525e97e448e48","timestamp":"2026-07-13T08:34:08.855Z","kind":"message","source_event_kind":"codex:response_item:message","role":"assistant","text":"Your instinct is right: this is not a preferable data model. It is a downgrade-compatibility shim.\n\n| Direction | Mechanism |\n|---|---|\n| New GitButler reads old snapshots | `VirtualBranches.default_target` remains deserializable |\n| New GitButler reads new snapshots | authoritative `project_meta.toml` |\n| Old GitButler reads new snapshots | synthetic `[default_target]` appended to snapshot TOML |\n\nSimply setting `VirtualBranches.default_target` no longer works because it is `#[serde(skip_serializing)]` in [virtual_branches_legacy_types.rs]([REDACTED:path]). Removing that attribute would let ordinary live metadata writes resurrect stale legacy targets via [storage.rs]([REDACTED:path]).\n\nSo [the concatenation]([REDACTED:path]) deliberately bypasses that rule only for the snapshot copy. Older versions ignore `project_meta.toml`, restore `virtual_branches.toml`, and expect its target there. The values still pass through the TOML serializer, so it is awkward rather than unsafe.\n\nMy judgment:\n\n- If restoring new snapshots after downgrading GitButler is not an explicit requirement, delete `SnapshotLegacyTarget` and the append logic. Keep the old-snapshot read fallback at [oplog.rs]([REDACTED:path]).\n- If downgrade restoration is required, the separate snapshot-only DTO is reasonable because it localizes the obsolete wire format. Re-enabling it on `VirtualBranches` would weaken the migration.\n- The compatibility is already incomplete: commit-only targets cannot be represented for old versions, as the test at [oplog.rs]([REDACTED:path]) acknowledges.\n\nAlso, `virtual_branches.default_target = None` before serialization is currently redundant because `skip_serializing` already guarantees that. No files changed.","tool_name":null,"tool_input":null,"source_record":{"timestamp":"2026-07-13T08:34:08.855Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"[REDACTED:entropy]","role":"assistant","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"[REDACTED:entropy]"},"phase":"final_answer"}}}